WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.868
-My first guests are

00:00:01.868 --> 00:00:03.300
two very talented people.

00:00:03.300 --> 00:00:04.667
He's a Super Bowl champion

00:00:04.667 --> 00:00:06.667
and she's
a Grammy-winning artist.

00:00:06.667 --> 00:00:09.400
Together, they're hosting
a vaccination awareness special

00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:11.067
called "Roll Up Your Sleeves,"

00:00:11.067 --> 00:00:14.767
which airs Sunday night
at 7:00 pm, here on NBC.

00:00:14.767 --> 00:00:17.801
Please welcome
Russell Wilson and Ciara!

00:00:17.801 --> 00:00:19.968
[ Cheers and applause ]
That's what I'm talking about!

00:00:19.968 --> 00:00:21.234
-Hey!
-Hey!

00:00:21.234 --> 00:00:24.133
-Look at you guys!
Ah!

00:00:24.133 --> 00:00:27.100
Russell, Ciara, thank you
so much for doing our show

00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:29.734
and coming on the show again.
I appreciate it.

00:00:29.734 --> 00:00:32.367
You were nice enough
to come on our show

00:00:32.367 --> 00:00:34.434
when we first started
doing it from home.

00:00:34.434 --> 00:00:37.167
I don't know if you remember
the last interview. Do you?

00:00:37.167 --> 00:00:38.834
-We do remember.
-We do remember.

00:00:38.834 --> 00:00:40.601
-We remember very vividly,
actually.

00:00:40.601 --> 00:00:44.267
I think your daughter actually
ran in and lost a tooth.

00:00:44.267 --> 00:00:46.133
-My daughter ran in.
She was so excited.

00:00:46.133 --> 00:00:47.434
She's like, "Dad, Dad, Dad!"

00:00:47.434 --> 00:00:51.200
Screaming and there was blood
all over her mouth.

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:52.734
[ Laughter ]

00:00:52.734 --> 00:00:53.801
She did.
She lost a tooth

00:00:53.801 --> 00:00:55.767
right in the middle
of our interview

00:00:55.767 --> 00:00:57.267
and you guys were
so nice to her

00:00:57.267 --> 00:00:58.868
and, clearly,
you're good parents.

00:00:58.868 --> 00:01:00.734
You were like,
"Oh, how'd you lose it?"

00:01:00.734 --> 00:01:02.200
And I'm like,
"Honey, no one else is going

00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:04.567
to think this is cute.
Because I'm your dad, so --"

00:01:04.567 --> 00:01:06.734
But there's just blood
gushing out and she's like,

00:01:06.734 --> 00:01:09.567
"I lost --" And I go,
"Just get out of here."

00:01:09.567 --> 00:01:10.801
[ Laughter ]
Go hide.

00:01:10.801 --> 00:01:12.834
Wait 'til the interview's over.

00:01:12.834 --> 00:01:15.000
-Anytime that happens,
it's always a good thing.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:16.834
-It's a big moment.
-Isn't her name Winnie, too?

00:01:16.834 --> 00:01:19.133
-Yes! Wait! We have --
-Yeah. Winnie, right?

00:01:19.133 --> 00:01:20.834
-I'm burying the lede, here.

00:01:20.834 --> 00:01:23.367
Congratulations
on your new baby! Come on!

00:01:23.367 --> 00:01:25.367
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Yeah.

00:01:25.367 --> 00:01:27.167
-Wait.
Get ready for this.

00:01:27.167 --> 00:01:30.367
You want to see a cute baby?
Get ready for this.

00:01:30.367 --> 00:01:32.667
This is little Win right here.

00:01:32.667 --> 00:01:34.534
-Aww!
-Look! Are you joking me?

00:01:34.534 --> 00:01:36.334
[ Laughs ]
-He's the best.

00:01:36.334 --> 00:01:38.234
-That is just precious.

00:01:38.234 --> 00:01:39.234
Oh, my God.

00:01:39.234 --> 00:01:41.200
The little sneakers.
Oh, my gosh.

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:44.167
[ Laughter ]
And what a great name, Win.

00:01:44.167 --> 00:01:45.234
-Yeah, Win Wilson.

00:01:45.234 --> 00:01:48.100
-Win Wilson.
Do you call him Winnie?

00:01:48.100 --> 00:01:50.300
-Sometimes I do say
Winnie the Pooh.

00:01:50.300 --> 00:01:53.300
We play off of Winnie the Pooh
with him, so, but, yeah.

00:01:53.300 --> 00:01:55.400
-I mean, you end up making
so many nicknames for your kids.

00:01:55.400 --> 00:01:57.100
I don't call my kids
by their names anymore.

00:01:57.100 --> 00:01:59.501
Like I call them
Noodle and Doodle.

00:01:59.501 --> 00:02:01.033
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:02:01.033 --> 00:02:03.200
-It's just crazy.

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:05.701
But how's the baby?
How is he?

00:02:05.701 --> 00:02:07.033
-He's amazing.
-Yeah.

00:02:07.033 --> 00:02:08.601
Win is so energetic.

00:02:08.601 --> 00:02:10.334
He's all over the place.

00:02:10.334 --> 00:02:13.501
I definitely think he has
dad genes all run through him.

00:02:13.501 --> 00:02:15.234
-Really?
-He's ready to play right now.

00:02:15.234 --> 00:02:17.234
He's ready to rock 'n' roll.
It's a lot of fun.

00:02:17.234 --> 00:02:19.100
Our hands are tied.
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:19.100 --> 00:02:21.801
You recently celebrated
an anniversary.

00:02:21.801 --> 00:02:24.601
March 26th marks six years

00:02:24.601 --> 00:02:27.400
to the day you two first met.

00:02:27.400 --> 00:02:29.434
What do you remember
about that day?

00:02:29.434 --> 00:02:31.267
-Oh, man, it was a special day,
first of all,

00:02:31.267 --> 00:02:34.934
It was Wisconsin vs. UNC
in the lead 8, actually,

00:02:34.934 --> 00:02:37.367
[ Laughter ]
and Wisconsin won that game.

00:02:37.367 --> 00:02:40.634
And I was supposed to actually
go to dinner with Ari, you know,

00:02:40.634 --> 00:02:42.701
and have a whole, you know,

00:02:42.701 --> 00:02:44.400
dinner and everything
around 7:30.

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:45.634
And I had texted Ci.

00:02:45.634 --> 00:02:47.033
I said, "Hey, can we meet up,

00:02:47.033 --> 00:02:48.400
you know, around 10:00, 10:30?"

00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:50.400
She said,
"Ah, well, you know, sorry.

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:53.000
I got to go to New York the next
morning around 4:00, 4:30."

00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:55.567
So, you know, if it's meant
to be, it's meant to be.

00:02:55.567 --> 00:02:57.634
I'm like, "Hold on a second.
This is meant to be."

00:02:57.634 --> 00:02:59.033
So, next thing I know, I said,
"Hey, alright,

00:02:59.033 --> 00:03:00.601
let's move the meeting
to 10:30."

00:03:00.601 --> 00:03:02.501
Next thing I know,
four and a half hours later,

00:03:02.501 --> 00:03:04.901
you know, I completely forgot
about the meeting

00:03:04.901 --> 00:03:06.767
and I fell in love that day...

00:03:06.767 --> 00:03:09.467
-Aww.
-...so that was one
of the best days.

00:03:09.467 --> 00:03:11.167
-We're actually both a lot
about eating as well

00:03:11.167 --> 00:03:14.434
because we were chatting
all night and it was special.

00:03:14.434 --> 00:03:15.734
-Yeah, good night.
-It was meant to be.

00:03:15.734 --> 00:03:18.133
Ciara, is this true?

00:03:18.133 --> 00:03:19.968
One of the first dates
that Russell took you

00:03:19.968 --> 00:03:22.100
was to the White House?

00:03:22.100 --> 00:03:23.133
-[ Laughs ]
-Yes, that's right.

00:03:23.133 --> 00:03:25.200
One of our first dates was

00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:29.300
to honor the
prime minister of Japan, Abe.

00:03:29.300 --> 00:03:31.534
And it was a special night.
It was really fun.

00:03:31.534 --> 00:03:33.901
It was very presidential.
[ Laughs ]

00:03:33.901 --> 00:03:35.300
But it's a good time.
It was,

00:03:35.300 --> 00:03:36.534
yeah, really, really memorable.

00:03:36.534 --> 00:03:39.501
-Yeah. Jimmy, anytime
you lead off with that,

00:03:39.501 --> 00:03:40.934
I have to level up
every time, now,

00:03:40.934 --> 00:03:42.767
so I'm trying to find new,
creative ways.

00:03:42.767 --> 00:03:44.601
So, you got any tips,
let me know.

00:03:44.601 --> 00:03:46.400
-How are you going to top dinner
at the White House?

00:03:46.400 --> 00:03:47.934
Gosh!
Unbelievable.

00:03:47.934 --> 00:03:51.067
But I heard there was
a dance party as well.

00:03:51.067 --> 00:03:52.467
-Yes, we did.
We had a good time,

00:03:52.467 --> 00:03:53.968
but that night
was a special night

00:03:53.968 --> 00:03:56.133
because, you know,
we were dancing.

00:03:56.133 --> 00:03:57.534
Prince was performing.

00:03:57.534 --> 00:04:00.701
Stevie Wonder gets up onstage
and just an amazing night.

00:04:00.701 --> 00:04:04.033
But the crazy thing is -- Yeah,
that's how it starts off, Jimmy.

00:04:04.033 --> 00:04:06.767
But then, fast-forward,
end of the night, it gets late

00:04:06.767 --> 00:04:08.100
and they got the DJ playing

00:04:08.100 --> 00:04:10.400
and they're playing
Beyoncé's song, you know,

00:04:10.400 --> 00:04:12.267
and they're talking about you
got to put a ring on it,

00:04:12.267 --> 00:04:14.667
"Single Ladies,"
and Obama comes up to me

00:04:14.667 --> 00:04:17.901
and Michelle's next to Ci
and Barack's next to me

00:04:17.901 --> 00:04:19.067
and, next thing you know,

00:04:19.067 --> 00:04:21.234
he's all in my face
with the ring --

00:04:21.234 --> 00:04:22.400
♪ You better put a ring on it ♪

00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:24.100
[ Laughter ]
And so I'm like, "Okay, well."

00:04:24.100 --> 00:04:27.400
Now, I'm now getting challenged
by Barack Obama, you know.

00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:28.934
The president of the
United States is telling me

00:04:28.934 --> 00:04:30.267
I got to put a ring
on this thing, so.
-Wow!

00:04:30.267 --> 00:04:32.734
Look at him!
Oh, my gosh!

00:04:32.734 --> 00:04:34.100
That is unbelievable.
-Good night.

00:04:34.100 --> 00:04:37.000
-Last time
we talked to you guys,

00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:40.667
we talked about your foundation,
the Why Not You Foundation,

00:04:40.667 --> 00:04:44.033
and, now, you have
a fashion house, okay?

00:04:44.033 --> 00:04:47.334
This is called the House of LR&amp;C

00:04:47.334 --> 00:04:49.067
-Yes.
-and with a percentage going,

00:04:49.067 --> 00:04:51.167
proceeds going
to your foundation.

00:04:51.167 --> 00:04:53.300
First of all, tell me
about the House of LR&amp;C.

00:04:53.300 --> 00:04:55.901
What does LR&amp;C stand for?

00:04:55.901 --> 00:04:58.467
-Well, LR&amp;C stands
for Love, Respect, &amp; Care

00:04:58.467 --> 00:05:01.133
and those are some
fundamental values

00:05:01.133 --> 00:05:02.501
that really meant
a lot to Russ and I.

00:05:02.501 --> 00:05:03.801
We were thinking about what
we were going to name

00:05:03.801 --> 00:05:06.100
our fashion house.
And it's our fashion house.

00:05:06.100 --> 00:05:08.400
It houses all of our fashion
brands that we're building out,

00:05:08.400 --> 00:05:10.133
Good Man Brand and Human Nature,

00:05:10.133 --> 00:05:11.534
our most recent brand
that we've launched,

00:05:11.534 --> 00:05:14.634
and where we team up with our
good friend Christine Day,

00:05:14.634 --> 00:05:15.801
who's a retail legend,

00:05:15.801 --> 00:05:17.334
and she's been helping us
run this thing.

00:05:17.334 --> 00:05:20.434
And the LR&amp;C also stands
for Love, Russell &amp; Ciara,

00:05:20.434 --> 00:05:22.601
so it's a double entendre
to the name.

00:05:22.601 --> 00:05:23.868
But it's all the values
that we're pouring

00:05:23.868 --> 00:05:26.767
into what we're building,
and also sustainability is

00:05:26.767 --> 00:05:28.200
at the foundation
of it all as well,

00:05:28.200 --> 00:05:30.901
so we're really proud of it
and it's been really fun.

00:05:30.901 --> 00:05:32.067
-It's so cool that you guys
are doing that.

00:05:32.067 --> 00:05:33.501
I think that's awesome.

00:05:33.501 --> 00:05:36.901
Not only that, but you're also
hosting this event Sunday,

00:05:36.901 --> 00:05:39.501
this Sunday at 7:00 pm on NBC.

00:05:39.501 --> 00:05:41.400
This is called
"Roll Up Your Sleeves."

00:05:41.400 --> 00:05:43.767
How'd you get involved
with this?

00:05:43.767 --> 00:05:46.200
-Well, our good friends at NBC
reached out to us

00:05:46.200 --> 00:05:48.467
and, of course,
Michelle Obama asks you to be

00:05:48.467 --> 00:05:50.200
a part of something,
you never say no.

00:05:50.200 --> 00:05:52.100
[ Laughter ]
And so, a cool opportunity

00:05:52.100 --> 00:05:53.868
to host a show and we want
to be a part

00:05:53.868 --> 00:05:55.567
of raising awareness
about the vaccine,

00:05:55.567 --> 00:05:57.033
everybody going out
and getting vaccinated.

00:05:57.033 --> 00:05:59.133
And it also airs the day
before vaccines

00:05:59.133 --> 00:06:02.167
are open to everyone,
which is super, super cool.

00:06:02.167 --> 00:06:03.968
And over 806 million people

00:06:03.968 --> 00:06:05.367
have already been
vaccinated to date,

00:06:05.367 --> 00:06:07.467
so, you know,
we're all moving together

00:06:07.467 --> 00:06:08.634
and we're all in this together

00:06:08.634 --> 00:06:10.501
and so we're just raising
awareness about it.

00:06:10.501 --> 00:06:12.300
-It's going to be fun,
just to be able to host this

00:06:12.300 --> 00:06:15.434
and encourage people
to try to keep everybody safe.

00:06:15.434 --> 00:06:17.100
-Yeah. Let's go.
-Yeah.

00:06:17.100 --> 00:06:19.300
I appreciate that.
Thank you guys for doing that.

